1. Overview & File Breakdown
The precision, Recall and F1-score module calculates fine-grained statistical performance metrics (True Positives, False Positives, False Negatives, Precision, Recall, and F1-score) for target classes
2. File-by-File Implementation Mechanics
o	PrecisionrecallF1_main.cpp: Driver script computing and printing precision, recall, and F1 percentages for target classes using cout.
o	example_ PrecisionrecallF1.cpp: Standalone example outputting detailed performance reports.
o	test_PrecisionrecallF1.cpp: Unit test asserting that calculated precision and recall values match hand-calculated baseline expectations.
3. Error Handling Strategies
	Zero-Denominator Protection: Explicitly checks whether denominators equal zero before performing division, safely defaulting metrics to 0.0 to prevent program crashes or NaN outputs.
	Input Validation: Checks pointer bounds and throws std::invalid_argument for null inputs.
4. Conclusion
The Precision, Recall, and F1-Score module rounds out the evaluation suite with deep statistical insight. By incorporating robust zero-denominator guards, it ensures mathematically sound and crash-resistant metric reporting across all classification scenarios.
